  "description": {
    "text": "A half deck released for the film Destiny Deoxys, first at Japan's Pokémon Centers on 17 July 2004 and in other shops from 14 August 2004. It holds Pokémon from the film, such as Sky's Rayquaza and Pokémon of LaRousse City, and the first card of a fourth-generation Pokémon, LaRousse's Munchlax, who is also on the coin.\n\nIts highlight is Sky-Splitting Deoxys, the first and only lenticular card released in Japan, whose picture, illustrator and attacks change with the viewing angle. Normal Forme and Attack Forme cards of Sky-Splitting Deoxys are also in the deck.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Movie Commemoration VS Pack: Sky-Splitting Deoxys (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 20 August 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260820044150/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Movie_Commemoration_VS_Pack:_Sky-Splitting_Deoxys_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A black \"Vs\" symbol at the bottom right",
    "sources": [
